00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:54.280
Rule number one, when you're naming what's working, the smaller, the better.

260
00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:58.880
Naming small things that are working in your life are weirdly powerful.

261
00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:02.540
You might try and say, breakfast is working pretty well,

262
00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:06.720
but the specificity and smallness of having muffins in the freezer

263
00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:10.020
and protein yogurt drinks in the fridge are working super well for everybody.

264
00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:15.980
The smaller the thing, the greater the opportunity for you to truly understand what is working.

265
00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:19.800
You can see the particular moving parts of the thing

266
00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:23.160
rather than just like a large, ambiguous category.

267
00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:25.540
So rule number one, the smaller, the better.

268
00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:31.100
Rule number two, when you're naming what's working, working doesn't mean perfect.

269
00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:33.000
We're naming what's working.

270
00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:34.300
We're not naming what's perfect.

271
00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:36.500
Very little is and very little will be.

272
00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:39.120
Perfect is relative and arbitrary anyway.

273
00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:44.540
So as you assess and decide what's working in your life, be kind about that word.

274
00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:46.460
Working doesn't mean perfect.

275
00:11:46.820 --> 00:11:47.780
It's working.

276
00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:50.800
It might be a little janky and how it's working, but it's working.

277
00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:52.400
Don't be so hard on yourself.

278
00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:57.660
Rule number three, when you're naming what's working, now isn't forever.

279
00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:02.660
What's working now might not and likely won't work forever.

280
00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:04.580
